{"content":[{"c":["UNLEAVENED BREAD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Bread made without leaven (yeast). In ancient times, bread makers used a piece of dough remaining from a former baking process, a piece that had fermented and developed a certain acid content—the yeast that caused bread to rise."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Bread used at the Jewish Passover and most other religious observances was, by the command of God, unleavened (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.15-20","r":"Exod.12.15-20","rawR":"Exod.12.15-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.15-20","value":"Exod.12.15-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 12:15-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.23.15","r":"Exod.23.15","rawR":"Exod.23.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.23.15","value":"Exod.23.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:15"},"). Only under certain conditions were the people permitted to use leavened bread for spiritual purposes (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.7.13","r":"Lev.7.13","rawR":"Lev.7.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.7.13","value":"Lev.7.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 7:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.23.17","r":"Lev.23.17","rawR":"Lev.23.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.23.17","value":"Lev.23.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:17"},"). This was largely owing to the fact that leaven generally symbolized evil; fermentation implied decay and corruption."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["With the exception of Jesus’ teaching on the kingdom of God (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.13.33","r":"Matt.13.33","rawR":"Matt.13.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.13.33","value":"Matt.13.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 13:33"},"), the NT also speaks of leaven with a negative connotation. Jesus warned of the leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.16.6","r":"Matt.16.6","rawR":"Matt.16.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.16.6","value":"Matt.16.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:6"},"); Paul exhorted believers to guard against that tiny bit of yeast—unhealthy values—that can work through a whole batch of dough (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.5.6-8","r":"1Cor.5.6-8","rawR":"1Cor.5.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.5.6-8","value":"1Cor.5.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 5:6-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Bread_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Bread_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Bread_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Bread"},"; ",{"href":"?item=FoodandFoodPreparation_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"FoodandFoodPreparation_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"FoodandFoodPreparation_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Food and Food Preparation"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Leaven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Leaven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Leaven_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Leaven"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"UnleavenedBread","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 12:15-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.12.15-20","rawQueryValue":"Exod.12.15-20","sourceRefExact":"Exod.12.15-20"},{"anchorText":"23:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.23.15","rawQueryValue":"Exod.23.15","sourceRefExact":"Exod.23.15"},{"anchorText":"Lv 7:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.7.13","rawQueryValue":"Lev.7.13","sourceRefExact":"Lev.7.13"},{"anchorText":"23:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.23.17","rawQueryValue":"Lev.23.17","sourceRefExact":"Lev.23.17"},{"anchorText":"Mt 13:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.13.33","rawQueryValue":"Matt.13.33","sourceRefExact":"Matt.13.33"},{"anchorText":"16:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.16.6","rawQueryValue":"Matt.16.6","sourceRefExact":"Matt.16.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 5:6-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.5.6-8","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.5.6-8","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.5.6-8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"24b37b80da7c84d229b5a119ec544ee738d5e9a05489462791603b99c5590657","sourceItemName":"UnleavenedBread","sourceItemOrder":13,"sourceMember":"Articles/U.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"UnleavenedBread","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Unleavened Bread","title":"Unleavened Bread","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}